  "body": "I'm trying to have a usb device communicate with the OS via WebUSB.\r\n\r\nMy device is a raspberry pi zero, configured with the Linux USB gadget. I installed a CDC-ACM serial gadget and I have been able to communicate with the device with WebUSB, with a small issue:\r\n\r\nThe OS cdc-acm driver picks the device, so when I try to claim the interface I get an error, saying the interface is busy. To make it work, I need to unbind the CDC-ACM driver from the device using the command line, or lie using fake USB descriptors.\r\n\r\nSince WebUSB is born to make device works from the browser, having to setup something in the OS goes against the initial goal. Shouldn't WebUSB offer an option to unclaim the device?\r\n\r\nSee related discussion with @gregkh on Linux-USB mailing list:\r\n\r\nhttps://marc.info/?l=linux-usb&m=151796814527081&w=2",
